# Astro Development

- Prefer `.astro` components and static HTML/CSS.
- Keep JavaScript minimal; hydrate only when interactivity requires it.
- Do not add React, Vue, Svelte, or other UI frameworks unless explicitly required.
- Prefer native browser APIs over libraries for small tasks.
- Keep dependencies minimal; explain briefly before adding any package.
- Do not add UI kits, animation libs, icon packs, or utility libs unless genuinely required.
- Prefer readable, maintainable components over abstractions.
- Avoid over-engineering; preserve Astro’s performance model.
- Do not install packages or start building UI until the user explicitly requests implementation.
